WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.280
In my Things You Missed episodes on the Final
Destination franchise, I’ve pointed out

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.410
some of the hidden signs of impending disaster.
In Final Destination 5, this caution sign

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:11.010
can be seen ahead of the bridge, and what
looks like a simple peeling of plastic from

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.950
wear and tear is actually a warning of the
titanic bridge collapse that would follow.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.480
As usual there would be connections to the
disaster that the franchise is based around,

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.279
the crash of Flight 180. The bus they are
on is from Rolland Coach Lines. Rolland is

00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:27.100
a french name, “that’s a French *** name!”
and the logo features a bird feather, a reference

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.220
to flight and the memorial of the Flight 180
crash.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.899
The video that plays inside the bus is from
180 Corporate Consulting, and the bus number

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:39.290
is 1282, the sum of whose digits add up to
13, the unlucky number that we’ve seen arise

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.180
in every Final Destination movie.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.570
The main character, Sam, also known as Nick
2.0, sees a vehicle labeled Tagert Logging

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:49.940
Truck No 2. Target is a reference to the Tagert
theater, an accident location in the fourth

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:54.600
movie, and No. 2 is a reference to Final Destination
2, which notably had a huge accident involving

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.608
a logging truck just like this one.

00:00:56.608 --> 00:01:00.270
And the license plate of this Chevrolet
matches Carter Horton’s car that gets destroyed

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:01.270
in the first movie.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:05.199
Then, there’s Nathan’s line about his
employee, Roy, which is another possible Death

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:06.199
omen.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.740
“I want him over. Even if it kills me.”

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:13.070
To learn all of FD5’s secrets, including
the clues about the movie’s twist ending,

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:17.188
stick around to the end of this video. This
video is sponsored by NordVPN.

00:01:20.829 --> 00:01:26.689
Oh my. Sound the alarm! Alert the media. Because
CZ is actually finishing a movie franchise

00:01:26.689 --> 00:01:28.630
he started on Things You Missed.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:33.289
“I’ve got to make sure that YouTube comes
down to tape this.”

00:01:33.289 --> 00:01:38.409
The fifth and final of the original tri-annual
Final Destination movies was directed by Steven

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:41.849
Quale, whose last name sounds like a combination
of a quesadilla and something you would put

00:01:41.849 --> 00:01:45.349
on your salad. This is why I should never
write these episodes while I'm hungry. Let’s

00:01:45.349 --> 00:01:46.873
get into the Things You Missed.

00:01:52.649 --> 00:01:57.359
The story begins outside the offices of Presage
Paper. The word presage is no accident, it’s

00:01:57.359 --> 00:02:01.399
defined as a sign or warning that something
(typically something bad) will happen. It’s

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:05.520
also probably no mistake that this is a paper
company, because the boss of Presage Paper,

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.750
a man named Dennis Lapman is played by actor
David Kochner, who many will recognize from

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:14.170
his role at the time in the US television
sitcom The Office, where he plays Tod Packer,

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.250
who is pretty much the same character as Dennis.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.939
PACKER: “Merry Christmas ***hole!”
MICHAEL: “No way! Ah, you’re kidding me.

00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:23.920
Packer! Yes!”

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.849
He also seems to have brought himself an Exec
of the Year mug, much like how Michael Scott

00:02:27.849 --> 00:02:30.591
has a mug that says World’s Best Boss in The Office.

00:02:30.591 --> 00:02:34.909
The license plates also tell us we’re back
in New York, where Final Destinations 1 and

00:02:34.909 --> 00:02:38.670
2 took place. Sam and his girlfriend Molly
are having some relationship issues.

00:02:41.084 --> 00:02:45.334
“Molly, your ticket’s cancelled. Tell
me that’s a mistake.”

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:48.235
“I was gonna tell you after this weekend.
It’s not working out Sam."

00:02:48.235 --> 00:02:50.510
“Well that was a waste of a travel ticket.”

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:54.370
If you’ve seen my previous episodes on the
other movies, you know the drill. Luck, chance

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.219
and fate are always referenced in these movies,
because being caught in a disaster is seen

00:02:58.219 --> 00:03:03.040
as bad luck, and many of the victims are superstitious.
Candice has a pair of lucky rubber bands.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:08.092
“Oh it’s just something I do to relax
me. And for luck.”

00:03:08.092 --> 00:03:11.340
...and it snaps right before her accident.
The news station that reports on the bridge

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.790
collapse is on channel 13, the unlucky number.
The survivors are referred to as the Lucky

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:16.790
8…

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.280
“And although they’ve been branded the
Lucky 8…”

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.409
Though, eight is not usually considered a
lucky number, as Bradley Donovan can probably

00:03:23.409 --> 00:03:27.670
attest to. Isaac steals a gift certificate
for Ming Yun Spa. Ming Yun is the concept

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:31.739
of personal life and destiny in Chinese folk
lore, and before his treatment, he rubs the

00:03:31.739 --> 00:03:35.950
Buddha statue’s belly, which is also seen as an omen of good luck. Ironically, it’s

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.370
that same statue that winds up being the end
of him.

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:42.409
Olivia also taints her own fortune shortly
before her demise, by knocking over a picture

00:03:42.409 --> 00:03:44.269
frame on her desk. More on that later.

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:47.970
The Coach Bus comes up onto the North Bay
Bridge, and we can see it’s a long way down

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.050
to the surface.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.069
“Computer generated and animated water.”

00:03:52.069 --> 00:03:56.499
Final Destination 5 also brings back the concept
of a recurring Death omen song, Dust in the

00:03:56.499 --> 00:04:00.799
Wind by Kansas. This may be a reference to
the tendency of Death to materialize in the

00:04:00.799 --> 00:04:04.999
form of a gust of wind. We’ve seen the winds
of Death in relation to many of the accidents,

00:04:04.999 --> 00:04:09.060
but perhaps none more than the bridge collapse,
which was said to be the result of high winds

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.069
and structural damage caused by the construction.

00:04:11.069 --> 00:04:14.379
“They chalk it up to high winds and structural
damage from the road construction.”

00:04:14.379 --> 00:04:15.980
“High winds?”

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:20.049
In the scene where the bridge gives way, there
are many undetected clues about how each survivor

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:24.440
would meet their fate. For example, Isaac
dies while laying on his stomach in the premonition,

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:28.260
and he would be in the same position at the
massage place when Death catches up with him.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:31.770
Olivia’s fate is essentially sealed once
she loses her glasses in the vision, a clue

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:35.651
about her real final moments which are spent
in a procedure to correct her vision. The

00:04:35.651 --> 00:04:39.190
premonition shows her surviving the bridge
fall, but ultimately being done in when a

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:43.751
car fall on her. Her actual doom is the opposite,
after her eye is mutilated by the laser, she

00:04:43.751 --> 00:04:47.500
does her best Aunt Maggie and falls down several
stories onto a car.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:51.030
Several characters have to make their way
across a steel beam to get to safety, a foreshadowing

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:55.310
of the balance beam accident that ultimately
got Candice bent over backwards. In the vision,

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.630
Candice does fall to her death, which she
technically does in the gym as well.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:02.970
Peter gets impaled by stakes, just as he is
when Sam skewers him A la Carte and Sam is

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:06.530
chopped in half, much like what happens to
Molly when she’s dissected by the wing of

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:10.210
the airplane. Nathan’s death isn’t really
foreshadowed in the vision, but there would

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:13.655
be a very interesting secret hidden in one
of his time cards.

