00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:23.349
The news reports that Presage Paper has 8 survivors,
but the other 17 employees perished in the

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:26.030
collapse. There must have been some people
stowed underneath, because I do not recall

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:28.410
seeing 23 people on that bus.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:31.470
Surprisingly, this movie doesn’t really
keep up with the tradition of the names of

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:35.370
the deceased being the name of crew members
on the movie. Only two of the last names matches

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:38.919
a name in the credits, and Johnson is one of
the most common American names.

00:06:38.919 --> 00:06:43.599
There are two graves in the background, that
be the graves of previous Final Destination

00:06:43.599 --> 00:06:47.270
characters. Carpenter could be the headstone
for Nora and Tim Carpenter from Final Destination

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:51.430
2 and Clarke was one of the police officers
from Final Destination 3… although, these

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:54.419
can't actually be their tombstones because those characters haven't died yet.

00:06:54.419 --> 00:06:58.240
While the crew reference easter eggs tradition
may have been let go, the tradition of something

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.621
wildly inappropriate happening at every funeral
goes strong.

00:07:03.909 --> 00:07:06.726
DENNIS: “Or Isaac Palmer.”
ISAAC: “Did he just say my name? 

00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:12.394
That's not funny.”
OLIVIA: "I know, I'm sorry. I just get weird with tragedies. I'm sorry.”

00:07:13.453 --> 00:07:15.912
NATHAN: “I see dead people.”

00:07:15.912 --> 00:07:19.485
This is, of course, a reference to the iconic
line from The Sixth Sense.

00:07:22.878 --> 00:07:25.240
“I see dead people.”

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:28.741
If you like references to freakin great 90s
movies, this is the entry for you, because

00:07:28.741 --> 00:07:32.389
another can be seen later at the office in
the form of these cubicle sticky notes spelling

00:07:32.389 --> 00:07:37.449
out “Always Be Closing,” iconic sales
mantra from Glengarry Glen Ross.

00:07:38.996 --> 00:07:49.660
“A - B - C.... A - Always. B - Be. C - Closing. Always
be closing, ALWAYS be closing!”

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:53.569
Of course, the most final chapter of the original
pentalogy of Final Destination would contain

00:07:53.569 --> 00:07:55.970
a fair share of references to the other films.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:59.319
When Sam visits Molly, she’s boiling water,
which was part of Valerie Lewton’s death

00:07:59.319 --> 00:08:02.840
in the first one; in the gymnastics scene
a potentially electrically charged puddle

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:06.610
creeps towards Candice’s foot like the puddle
in Tod Waggner’s bathroom; Sam’s cubicle

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:11.199
has a toy motorcycle, similar to Eugene’s
motorcycle in FD2, and the motto “Born to

00:08:11.199 --> 00:08:14.569
Ride” references the opening of each movie
which all feature disasters during a ride

00:08:14.569 --> 00:08:17.719
of some kind and Isaac flirts with a girl
on the phone named Kimber, 

00:08:17.719 --> 00:08:19.660
"Tell me it's the Kimber from last Tuesday."

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.620
this could have maybe been Kimberly Corman from Final Destination
2.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:26.469
Also, this has nothing to do with the story
at all, but did anyone notice as Sam is getting

00:08:26.469 --> 00:08:30.379
out of work, there’s this truck just completely
bastardizing the parking job? I mean, that

00:08:30.379 --> 00:08:33.100
person is almost completely up on the curb,
what the hell?

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:36.830
Speaking of hell, there are usually a lot
of references to Hell or the devil in relation

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:40.420
to deaths. I think there’s only one new
one in this movie. It comes when the rogue

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:44.141
factory guy Roy fails to take Mr. Krabs’s
warning into account…

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.635
“They're back! They're back I tell ya! The hooks! The hooks!”

00:08:49.635 --> 00:08:53.540
...And gets himself Bobby Dagened right through
the skull. The end of “the hook!” pokes

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:57.480
through the top of his skull like a devil’s
horn. After seeing this, Peter is very…

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:00.850
shall we say… curious, about the circumstances
of the accident.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.223
PETER: “Did you or didn’t you?”
SAM: “Hey Peter, calm down--”

00:09:03.223 --> 00:09:05.590
PETER: Did you or didn’t you? Did you or
didn’t you?”

00:09:06.853 --> 00:09:08.020
DID YOU OR DIDN'T YOU?!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.850
NATHAN: “Yes. I think I did.”
I never understood why he would say that.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:14.910
Anyway, the first tragedy after escaping the
bridge is Candice’s gymnastics mishap. She

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:19.000
speaks with her boyfriend before going on,
and walks out from Section 108 in the stands,

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.300
an anagram of the cursed flight number: 180.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:24.780
Earlier I mentioned the wind being a symbol
that Death is among the characters, and we’ve

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:28.580
seen it in many forms in the series, starting
with the fan in Alex Browning’s bedroom. In

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:31.820
the gymnastics scene, we see a fan brought
in because the air conditioning is broken

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:34.210
and it contributes to taking out Candice.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:38.470
Another bad sign that can be found in the
scene is an AC plug, which looks kind of like a skull.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:44.070
The ambulance that shows up is U1575. U is
the 21st letter of the alphabet, so if you

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:50.130
add that to the other digits, 1+5+7+5, you
get 39, which matches the amount of Mt. Abraham

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:52.570
High School students who pass away on Flight
180.

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:57.340
The next day at the office, not that The Office,
some of the remaining Presage employees return

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:00.730
to work. In each movie, I’ve mentioned how
the character names correspond with filmmakers

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:04.760
who had an impact on the horror genre. It’s
here we find out about a few more.

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:09.450
Olivia Castle is named after the great William
Castle, Peter Friedkin after the great William

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:13.830
Friedkin, and Candice Hooper after the great
Tobe Hooper. Olivia’s eye doctor is named

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:18.340
Dr. Leonetti. This may be a reference to John Leonetti a notable horror movie cinematographer

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:20.720
horror films than a director that would go
on to direct five horror films in a row after

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:25.570
this. Isaac Palmer was named after Betsy Palmer
who is most well known as Pamela Voorhees.

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:29.040
Isaac does some snooping around the office
and steals a gift certificate from his late

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:32.551
co-worker. The expiration date is

00:10:32.551 --> 00:10:35.330
6/30/01. If we
multiply 6x30x1 we get the number that’s

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:39.980
come up time and time again: one hundred seventy
nine. I’m just kidding. It’s 180.

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:44.640
The certificate number also ends in 810 which
is an anagram of 180. Isaac hurts his finger

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:48.160
while retrieving it, just as Sam did on the
bus and on the plane, meaning that this would

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.440
be a sign that Isaac’s hours are numbered.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:54.230
Nathan brings up a case of adult beverages.
If you watched my other Final Destination

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:58.080
videos, you already know what’s coming.
It’s a 6-pack of Hice Pale Ale, the fizzy

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:02.640
but fatal refreshment that foreshadowed disasters
in the last 3 Final Destination movies.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:06.717
But the office would contain another important
Final Destination callback.

00:11:15.125 --> 00:11:19.710
FD5 lacks the volume of crew reference easter
eggs that the other movies have, but I did

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:24.190
spot one more in the Presage office. In Olivia’s
work area, there is a memorandum to the board

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:28.620
of directors from Adrian Hrydak. He is Final
Destination 5’s graphic designer.

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:32.140
I already mentioned Olivia’s broken picture
frame, but what I didn’t bring up is the

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:36.270
photo itself. It’s a ride photo from Devil’s
Flight, the roller coaster that would crash

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:40.540
5 years later during the events of Final Destination
3. They claim it’s the World’s Scariest

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:45.020
Roller Coaster. The movie is set in 2000 about
2 weeks before Millenium Force would open,

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:47.850
but I’d still probably have to give it to
Oblivion at that point in time.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:53.880
The next death is Isaac’s at the massage
place. “Yum yum dim sum!” And the only

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:57.280
other thing I’ll say about this is that
the no cell phones sign seen in the lobby

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:01.180
may count as an actual warning from Death,
considering that his phone is actually what

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:02.470
causes the fire.

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:06.450
After that is Olivia, at the Eastfield Laser
Eye Center, and her sign comes when she’s

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:10.350
squeezing the teddy bear for comfort and it’s
eye pops off. The same happens to her not

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:14.690
long after. Out of every scene in the franchise,
I think this is the fatality that affected

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:15.700
me most.

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:19.080
Sam recalls his vision to try to remember
the order that they were supposed to die in,

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:21.540
where we see, probably my favorite part.

00:12:22.376 --> 00:12:23.518
“AHHHHHH!”

00:12:23.518 --> 00:12:27.398
Why did they do that? Don’t they know that
slowing stuff down makes it funny?

00:12:27.398 --> 00:12:32.630
“AHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH!”

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:36.960
The next death is supposed to be Nathan, who’s
still having problems with an employee named Roy.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:41.520
He does a little snooping, using security
camera 32, the reverse of 23, as in Route

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:46.740
23. Also, just gotta say, for a security camera,
that definition is ****ing incredible. Look

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:51.020
at that. Most security cameras you can barely
even see Faze Bank’s bald spot, but on this

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.280
thing you can zoom right into the hairs on
Roy’s chin.

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:58.041
I gotta get me a camera like that. The DX8100.
It’s probably another anagram of the flight

00:12:58.041 --> 00:13:00.430
number 180. With an extra 0 tacked on.

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:03.940
The finale involves Peter coming into the
restaurant that Sam works at to take Molly’s

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:07.690
life so that he can theoretically add her
years to his own. Don’t get me wrong,

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:11.073
I love this scene. It’s very satisfying
to have an actual antagonist in these movies

00:13:11.073 --> 00:13:16.120
after nearly 5 movies. I just think the way
it all goes down is kind of hilarious. He

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:20.430
just invites himself in, pours himself a huge
glass of wine and then goes all Badlands Chugs

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:22.470
on it.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:28.510
And then Peter chases them into the kitchen
and… what, why is he turning on all the

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:33.320
fryers? Is he planning on deep frying Molly?
This is gonna be the best kill ever.

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:39.790
WHA! Do! It! Do! It!

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:44.070
As you may know, two thirds of all Final Destination
deaths are involve water or liquid. I think

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:46.850
this comment on my FD4 episode puts it best.

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:51.010
“Water is the source of life on this planet.
Without liquid water, we would not be here.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:53.470
It is fitting that a liquid starts all the
death.”

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:56.881
The movie started when The North Bay Bridge
collapsed into the water. Candice’s final

00:13:56.881 --> 00:14:00.660
college practice would become her final ever
practice thanks in part to the dripping water

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:04.580
from the air conditioner. Isaac didn’t exactly
get his happy ending massage, because the

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:08.930
bottle of disinfectant alcohol falls, starting
a typical Final Destination flammable liquid

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:13.610
incident. Olivia’s fun and games end when
her water, or rather, her Woda, spills onto

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:17.940
the outlet, causing the laser surgery machine
to malfunction. Sam and Molly’s plane crashes

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:21.240
into the Atlantic Ocean, and Nathan meets
his fate at a bar.

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:25.190
Of course, whenever I talk about Final Destination
5, people tell me how they were blown away

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:31.010
by that twist ending. Pun slightly intended.
Five was actually my first Final Destination

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:34.770
movie, because my friends told me you don’t
have to watch them in order. LIARS. So I had

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:38.510
no idea what was going on when they boarded
Flight 180 at the end, and I was kinda pissed

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:40.250
when I found out that it was ruined for me just so we could watch that movie that night.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:45.860
But upon rewatching, I noticed at least 9
different signs, some of which may be kind

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:50.190
of obvious, that Final Destination 5 was in
fact a prequel, not a sequel.

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:53.880
I’ll start with the opening credits. They
contain a montage of the other disasters we’ve

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:58.230
seen in the franchise, and when Flight 180
blows up, it emits this metal beam in a V-shape.

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:02.510
V is the roman numeral for five. Final Destination
5 would contain Flight 180.

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:06.180
We’ve got to take into account the title
of the lasts movie. It would be a bit strange

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:10.490
to make a movie called The Final Destination,
only to follow it up with a sequel a few years

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:16.300
later. However, making FD5 a prequel allows
The Final Destination to remain The Final

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:17.300
Destination chronologically.

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:21.080
Sam is an aspiring chef, and the next clue
comes when he reveals that his restaurant

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.840
wants to send him to an apprenticeship in
Paris.

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:27.100
“They want to send me to the flashship restaurant
in Paris for who knows how long?”

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:32.950
Flight 180 was a trip to Paris, France. The
restaurant he works is Le Cafe Miro 81. This

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:36.860
is the very same name as the restaurant whose
dislodged sign took out Carter Horton at the

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:40.180
end of the first Final Destination. Had he
ever made it to that job, he would have been

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:41.960
working at that very same restaurant.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:45.940
Then there’s the return of William Bludworth.
I went more into detail on this in my Horror

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:49.490
History episode on Bludworth, but basically,
he stops showing up after Final Destination

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.790
2, so his presence may suggest that we’re
actually in the past.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:56.050
More evidence that we’re at the dawn of
a new millennium can be found in the gymnasium

00:15:56.050 --> 00:16:01.761
at Westdale College where recent looking championship
banners are hanging from 1994 and 1998, but

00:16:01.761 --> 00:16:03.280
nothing past the year 2000.

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:07.420
Then in the office, there are a couple of
clues. The first is more of a bad omen. A

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:11.440
miniature model of the Volée aircraft can
be seen sitting on the cubicle walls, and

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:16.480
when Isaac steals Robert’s spa certificate,
the expiration date can clearly be seen: it’s

00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:21.910
in 2001, and when he tries to use it, it works,
implying that 2001 has not yet arrived.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:25.430
Later on, in Nathan’s office, we see the
actual date as he’s collecting time cards

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:30.200
for the week ending in April 30th 2000. This
is just 2 weeks before the date of the Volée

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:34.350
Flight 180 crash, which took place on May
13th, 2000 in the sequel universe.

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:37.980
As I’ve discussed before, there are two
continuities. In the original, the crash takes

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:43.049
place in 1999, in all the sequels, it takes
place in 2000.

00:16:43.049 --> 00:16:49.700
“I have thought a lot about that somewhere Alex. It exists, that place.”

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:53.650
So the day of the flight arrives, and Sam
and Molly take their seats in Row 23, there’s

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:55.070
that number from FD2 again.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:58.640
I did go back to the first movie to see if
the people sitting in those seats resembled

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:02.350
Sam and Molly at all. They don’t. There’s
a brown haired man in Molly’s seat and a

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:06.209
brunette woman in Sam’s. Which begs the
question: why didn’t they just cast character

00:17:06.209 --> 00:17:09.579
who look like these, rather than cast someone
who looks exactly like Nick from the last

00:17:09.579 --> 00:17:13.309
movie? None of the other passengers resemble
the passengers from the original Flight 180,

00:17:13.309 --> 00:17:16.000
for example, this is where Billy Hitchcock
should be.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:20.040
Actually, there are a lot of inconsistencies,
like how the plane is now 1 row shorter than

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:24.470
it was in the first movie. Or how the gate
number on Sam’s travel ticket is H6, but

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:29.190
we clearly see it’s Gate 46 in the first
movie. He’s seated in 23J. According to

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:33.170
the way the seats were mapped in the original,
he should actually have 23B.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:36.899
These could be seen as mistakes, and they
may be, but these small changes can be explained

00:17:36.899 --> 00:17:40.590
away with this idea that the sequel universe
changes little details from the original.

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:44.779
The final signs for Sam come too late. He
once again hears the Death omen song from

00:17:44.779 --> 00:17:48.460
the opening, Dust in the Wind, and Molly’s
magazine has an ad for Eastfield Laser Eye

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:52.259
Center where Olivia died. You’d think the
ensuing malpractice suit might have gotten

00:17:52.259 --> 00:17:53.399
them shut down.

00:17:53.399 --> 00:17:57.860
The final scene shows the final survivor,
Nathan, attending the memorial for Roy. Dust

00:17:57.860 --> 00:18:00.093
in the Wind can be heard playing in the background…

00:18:00.093 --> 00:18:02.162
🎵 Nothin' lasts forever but the earth and sky 🎵

00:18:02.162 --> 00:18:06.379
...and in one of the photos on the shrine,
we see that Roy is a fan of race car number

00:18:06.379 --> 00:18:10.679
6, the car that causes the big speedway accident
in Final Destination 4.

00:18:10.679 --> 00:18:14.190
There’s another FD4 reference, when this
guy tells Nathan that Roy didn’t have long

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:15.660
to live anyway.

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:18.450
“Life’s a b****.”

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:21.710
We saw this same phrase on the back of someone’s
shirt at the race track.

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:25.700
Finally, before the franchise would be laid
to rest for the next decade, they just had

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:28.006
to squeeze in one last Hice Pale Ale logo.

00:18:29.679 --> 00:18:33.400
There has been talk of a Final Destination
6, and I’m going to be doing a video breaking

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:37.650
down the possibilities for that new sequel.
So, make sure you’re subscribed to CZsWorld

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:42.179
for new horrors every week, ring the deathbell
for notifications, and I will see you in the

00:18:42.179 --> 00:18:48.799
next one. Assuming we both survive. If you
want to beat Death, use a facemask and social

00:18:48.799 --> 00:18:50.151
distancing.

